bias_risk_comments:
The study claims that "reindeer were the only grazers in the areas chosen for
this study; neither microtine herbivores (Mehlum 1990;
Henttonen et al. 2001) nor geese were present." While this might be true for the duration of the survey period in 2000, other species might have been present before and contributed to overall herbivory given that exclosures were built in 1978.

